    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A rare opportunity to acquire Benevenagh, a magnificent 4-bedroom end of terrace Victorian residence in the heart of Greystones Village, one of the town's most desirable locations, The Old Burnaby.\r\n\r\nBenevenagh is a home of exceptional character and fascinating history, having been the former home of legendary Irish musician Ronnie Drew, founding member of The Dubliners. This wonderful connection adds a unique sense of provenance to an already special property.\r\nBeautifully renovated while retaining its original Victorian character, the property combines generous proportions, high ceilings and an abundance of period detail with a superb contemporary specification. The result is a warm, elegant and highly individual family home presented in excellent condition.\r\n\r\nOccupying one of the village's most sought-after addresses, Benevenagh places boutique shops, cafés, award-winning restaurants, the marina, beaches, harbour and DART station all within a short stroll. Combining the charm of a thriving coastal village with outstanding convenience, Greystones continues to be one of Ireland's most sought-after places to call home."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Hall\r\nBright and welcoming, with a feature original hardwood staircase, custom-made Alan Brown seating/storage bench, attractive herringbone flooring, cast-iron radiator, understairs storage and attractive ceiling coving with wall panelling throughout\r\n\r\nSitting Room\r\nA beautifully proportioned south-facing reception room featuring upgraded double-glazed sash windows and wall panelling throughout. High ceiling with ornate coving and centre rose. Feature original fireplace with wood-burning stove and slate hearth. Traditional cast-iron radiator.\r\n\r\nLiving Room\r\nInterconnecting with the sitting room, this elegant reception room features an Alan Brown fitted alcove units with smart lighting. Ornate coving and ceiling rose, and a fireplace with slate inset and brass-trimmed surround incorporating a cast-iron wood burning stove. Traditional cast-iron radiator.\r\n\r\nKitchen / Dining / Family Area\r\nA superb open-plan space and the true heart of the home, showcasing a state-of-the-art Alan Brown kitchen with custom-built banquette seating and work/homework built in unit. Wide plank wood flooring. The kitchen features polished stone worktops and a centre island incorporating a Bora hob with built-in extractor fan.\r\n\r\nA comfortable lounge area within the open-plan space is currently used as a third family room and features a gas stove. Sliding door with electric motorised blinds leads directly to the well-maintained garden and stone patio, creating an excellent space for family living and alfresco dining. The kitchen provides an extensive range of high- and low-level units, top-of-the-range appliances and cleverly designed pantry. \r\n\r\nUtility area\r\nPlumbed for washing machine with provision for dryer, fitted units for storage.\r\n\r\nShower Room/Boot Room\r\nImpressive in both size and design, tiled floor, modern style WC and whb. Heated towel rail, built-in storage and electric Foxy dry indoor unit. Door leads out to the rear garden.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor Return\r\nFirst return with attractive arched landing. Wall panelling.\r\nLarge shelved hotpress.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 \r\nLarge fitted wardrobe. Old fashioned cast iron radiator. Sash window with view to the rear garden. Original fireplace. \r\n\r\nShower Room\r\nBeautifully appointed shower room featuring a tiled floor, traditional-style WC and whb with complementary traditional-style taps. A wall-mounted mirror with integrated lighting, heated towel rail and recessed lighting add a contemporary touch, while the generous step-in shower is fitted with a sliding glass door. A frosted sash window provides natural light and privacy.\r\n\r\nSeparate WC\r\nTiled floor with traditional-style WC and wash hand basin. Wall-mounted mirror and recessed lighting.\r\n\r\nSecond Floor\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 – Master Bedroom \r\nGenerously proportioned bedroom featuring an extensive range of fitted wardrobes. Original fireplace, with tiled sides and hearth, provides an attractive focal point, complemented by a traditional cast-iron radiator, picture rail and plantation shutters.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3\r\nWell-proportioned bedroom with a large sash window, extensive built-in wardrobes and traditional cast-iron radiator. An original fireplace and picture rail add further period character.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4\r\nBright and inviting bedroom featuring a large sash window, built-in wardrobe and traditional cast-iron radiator.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\nTo the Front\r\nSouth-facing front garden with limestone paving with granite edging leading to the front door. The garden is beautifully finished with Ballylusk stone and a stylish rattan seating area, creating an inviting outdoor space. The property also benefits from an electric car charging point, outdoor tap and external power sockets. Outdoor lighting. Gated side access leads to the rear garden, with secure keypad entry.\r\n\r\nTo the Rear\r\nThe rear walled garden features a paved patio area with an outdoor electric heater, providing an ideal space for year-round entertaining and al fresco dining. Beyond the patio is a well-maintained artificial lawn with ground and wall mounted lighting. The garden also benefits from a garden shed, outdoor tap and external power sockets. The rear garden has access to Burnaby Lane by way of keypad gate."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Double glazed sash windows throughout with plantation shutters\r\nElectric car charging point \r\nExtension and renovation completed in 2020\r\nNew roof to front and rear completed in 2020\r\nNew Alan Brown kitchen installed in 2020\r\nBER Rating C \r\nOrnate tiled entrance porch\r\nHigh ceilings, coving, picture rails and ceiling roses, faithfully reflecting the original period detail\r\nLight Wave – Smart light system\r\nRecessed lighting\r\nOriginal internal doors with detailed architraves\r\nAttractive herringbone flooring throughout the hall, sitting room and living room\r\nPolished stone worktops\r\nCentre island with Bora hob and built-in extractor fan\r\nMiele oven and warming drawer\r\nAga gas-fired range\r\nAlan Brown custom-built work/homework bench\r\nTraditional cast-iron radiators\r\nHigh-specification bathrooms with pumped showers and heated towel rails\r\nOriginal fireplaces with inset cast-iron wood-burning stoves\r\nGas-fired central heating\r\nOutdoor tap and external power sockets\r\nFitted wardrobes throughout all bedrooms\r\nUtility/boot room with extensive fitted storage"
      },
